:name: Zigbee 4.0 Light (real SDK firmware) — MG21 boot
:description: Boots the real, from-source-built Silicon Labs Zigbee 4.0 light firmware (zigbee_z4_light, part EFR32MG21A020F1024IM32) on the emulated MG21 platform. This is a full-stack firmware with a CLI (network-creator/network-steering), unlike the stripped vuln application ELFs — intended as the vehicle for a real over-the-air test once the radio model drives RAIL bring-up.
#
# Build: `make -f zigbee_z4_light.Makefile ARM_GCC_DIR=/usr/local -j4` with the
# system arm-none-eabi-gcc 9.3.1, after (1) replacing -flto=auto/-fwhole-program
# with -fno-lto (the shipped stack .a libs are FAT LTO objects built with a much
# newer GCC — LTO bytecode v8926 — so LTO must be off; the real machine code in
# the fat objects links fine), and (2) removing binutils-2.35 `(READONLY)`
# section attrs from autogen/linkerfile.ld. ELF: __Vectors=0x4000, entry 0x501d.
#
# BOOT STATUS (2026-07-13): runs real SL reset/CRT/CMU code; passes HFXO clock
# init after the SiLabs_HFXO_2 MG21 fix (releaseFsmLockOnDisableOnDemand). Then
# reaches RAIL radio init (~0x24dce) and busy-waits on an FRC DMA-completion
# handshake (FRC.IF bit14 @0xB8004000) that the SiLabs_xG24/xG22 radio model does
# not yet drive. Reaching the CLI prompt requires radio-model RAIL bring-up work
# (FRC DMA-complete flags, synth lock, RAC transitions, sequencer image) — a
# larger emulation effort, tracked separately.

$bin?=@scripts/silabs-vuln/z4light.elf
$vtor?=0x4000
include @scripts/silabs-vuln/boot_mg21.resc

# CLI is on USART0 (VCOM). Uncomment to watch it once RAIL bring-up is modelled.
# showAnalyzer sysbus.usart0

emulation RunFor "1"
echo ">>> PC after 1s (real firmware; ~0x24dce = RAIL init busy-wait until radio model drives FRC DMA-complete):"
sysbus.cpu PC
